\section{Conclusion}
\label{sec:conclusion}

Across 10 prompt-chain configurations spanning six architecture families (1B--8B), $\Kempirical \leq 2$ for all web text sources ($\theta{=}0.60$); arXiv reaches $\Kempirical{=}3$ across three families, with bootstrap resampling confirming stability (8/10 perfectly consistent; Table~\ref{tab:bootstrap_kstar}).
This one-wash laundering effect concentrates exploitable signal at the 0v1 boundary; binary curation minimizes MMLU degradation ($-$0.77\,pp vs.\ $-$1.53\,pp), and cross-model transfer retains 80--92\% of in-domain accuracy, supporting deployment without retraining.
Extending $\Kempirical$ to 13B+ scale, closing the $\Kempirical$--$\Ktheory$ gap, and bridging prompt-chain to retrain-chain boundaries remain open.

